---
type: journal
title: Muse Wonder 1.0 in the Meta catalog and Muse Code session commands
timestamp: 2026-10-19
---

# Scope

User supplied the Muse Wonder model card (https://research.meta.ai/static/muse-wonder-model-card)
and asked for Muse Code support at the Codex/Claude level, naming SSE, MCP and
chunked compaction. No live session was restarted.

# Model facts (official documentation, fetched 2026-10-19)

- `muse-wonder-1.0` is the Model API id; Standard mode only.
- 1,048,576-token context; input text, image, video, audio, PDF; output text.
- Reasoning effort from `minimal` to `max`.
- Muse Wonder Full is Muse Code/subscription-only and has no Model API id, so
  it is deliberately not registered.
- Not available in South Korea on Model API or in Muse Code (availability
  note in https://dev.meta.ai/docs/models).

# Changes

- `providers/meta.py`: `MUSE_WONDER_MODEL = "muse-wonder-1.0"` joins the
  provider's custom models and fallback list; a Wonder Codex catalog carries
  the card's input modalities and reasoning levels. Muse Spark profiles are
  unchanged; the profile lookup now uses a per-model catalog map.
- `config_migrations.py`: `meta_muse_wonder_100_20261019` appends the model to
  an existing saved Meta catalog once and never changes the selected model.
- `channel_compact_injection.py`: Muse joins `NEW_SESSION_COMMANDS` (`/new`)
  and `GOAL_RUNTIMES` (`/goal clear`); `/compact` was already runtime-neutral.
- `muse_runtime_context.py`: the interactive launch passes
  `session_command_runtime="muse"` to the channel proxy, so a queued session
  command can be typed into that terminal.

# Already present before this change

- Channel SSE delivery: Muse launches already run through the channel proxy
  (`enable_channels=True`, bracketed-paste wake), and the transcript repository
  already reads `~/.local/share/muse/sessions`.
- MCP: `muse_mcp.py` merges the router's `mcpServers` entry into
  `~/.config/muse/settings.json`.

# Not done

- Muse chunked compaction is not wired. The router's semantic map/reduce keys
  off a recognised compact request; Muse's `/compact` request shape has not
  been captured, and inventing a marker would misclassify ordinary turns.
  This needs a real routed Muse `/compact` capture before implementation.
- No live Muse launch was run for this change; verification is the focused
  unit suites.